FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] tests/bench/mod.rs:297-302 (with Display at tests/bench/mod.rs:104-108) — an oversized size is refused by `ensure_size_supported` and returned as `BenchError::BudgetExceeded`, whose Display says the workload "did not finish within its {n}s budget". The workload never started, and for the sub-second budgets the tests actually use (1ms/20ms) the message prints "its 0s budget". A user running `rb-bench fibonacci 20000000` is told a falsehood about elapsed work — a misleading failure channel in a phase whose whole point is clean failure. The tests (`tests/bench_test.rs:266-288`, and `tests/bench/mod.rs:645-655`) only pin the variant, not the message, so this is not contradicted by a test — but the fix should either make the Display truthful ("size N exceeds the checkable maximum M for 'fibonacci'") or add a distinct `SizeTooLarge { workload, size, max }` variant and update those two tests.
2. [MAJOR] tests/bench/mod.rs:437-453 — the primary documented entry point, `rb-bench` with no arguments (run all four, print the table, write `BENCH.md`), is untested. Every `run_cli` call in `tests/bench_test.rs:365-399` passes one or more arguments; nothing exercises the no-arg branch or the `std::fs::write` failure branch at line 447. This is exactly the branch the phase exists to deliver, and a regression that writes a wrong/empty file or returns the wrong exit code there would not be caught. Make the output path injectable (a `run_cli_with_path` used by both `run_cli` and a test writing to a temp dir) and assert the no-arg path writes a parseable file.
3. [MINOR] tests/bench/mod.rs:427-431 — `run_all` passes `DEFAULT_BUDGET` (60s) to each workload individually, so the no-arg CLI can block for up to 240s before any error, while `REPORT.md` and the `DEFAULT_BUDGET` doc (tests/bench/mod.rs:19-24) present "a 60-second self-enforced budget" as a single bound. Use one deadline (`Instant` + remaining time) across the run, or state that it is per workload.
4. [MINOR] tests/bench/mod.rs:32-37,59,292-304 — the per-workload `max_size` boundary is never tested: `edge_oversized_references_are_refused_before_allocation` (tests/bench_test.rs:266-288) only uses values far above the limit, so nothing pins `max_size` accepted / `max_size + 1` refused. Relatedly, `MAX_FIBONACCI_SIZE = 10_000_000` lets `expected_fibonacci` run into f64 infinity (fib overflows f64 around n≈1477), and `Expected::matches` uses `want == got`, so `inf == inf` is accepted as a "verified" answer. Add boundary tests and either cap Fibonacci where f64 is exact or reject non-finite expected values.
5. [MINOR] tests/unreviewed_work_ack_test.rs:254 vs 283-295 — the new `"resume phase-073:"` prefix is acknowledged with `DELIVERY_REASON`, but that reason enumerates only phase-084, phase-063 and phase-088, so the audit now records an acknowledgement whose text does not describe the phase-073 bench harness it is accepting. Extend `DELIVERY_REASON` (and the "in-flight phases" comment at 245-251) to name phase-073's files, or the audit data is inaccurate for the commit it tolerates.
6. [STYLE] tests/bench/mod.rs:65-70 vs 109-117 — `WrongAnswer` renders the expected text with `{:?}` (quoted) but the actual value with `Display` (unquoted), so a text mismatch reports e.g. `expected "\"ab\"", actual ab`. Render both the same way so the error is readable.

REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 6
